  "name": "Fillet of John Dory with Olives, Capers and Rosemary",
  "text": "Fillet of John Dory with Olives, Capers and Rosemary\n\nPreparation time: 10 minutes\n\nYield: 2\n\nIngredients\n\n2 fillets of John Dory,\n\n25 ml extra virgin olive oil,\n\n2 new potatoes,\n\n1 anchovy fillet (cut lengthways into thin slivers),\n\n1 1/2 pieces of sun dried tomato (roughly chopped),\n\nroughly chopped flat leaf parsley,\n\n2 very small vine ripened tomatoes (skinned, quartered and deseeded),\n\n4 pitted and halved black olives,\n\n6 nonpareil capers,\n\nleaves from 1” rosemary.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Preheat the grill to high.\n\n2. Halve each fillet diagonally. Brush with olive oil and season. Place skin side up on a baking sheet.\n\n3. Cut the potato into quarters and cook in boiling salted water until tender. Drain and return to the pan.\n\n4. Add the anchovies, sun dried tomatoes, parsley, fresh tomatoes, olives capers, rosemary, and oil. Warm through and season.\n\n5. Grill the fish for 3-4 minutes until barely cooked.\n\n6. Pour the sauce over the fish.",
  "prepTime": "PT10M",
